{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Never average down a losing position.", "source": "book:livermore", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["risk", "trade_mgmt", "rule:liv-01"], "author": "Edwin Lef\u00e8vre / Jesse Livermore", "triggers": ["drawdown_pct>3"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Cut losses quickly; let winners run.", "source": "book:livermore", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["risk", "trade_mgmt", "rule:liv-02"], "author": "Edwin Lef\u00e8vre / Jesse Livermore", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "The big money is in the big swing \u2014 sit tight in a winning trend.", "source": "book:livermore", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "trend", "rule:liv-03"], "author": "Edwin Lef\u00e8vre / Jesse Livermore", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Markets are never wrong, opinions often are.", "source": "book:livermore", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "rule:liv-04"], "author": "Edwin Lef\u00e8vre / Jesse Livermore", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Don't trade every day; wait for setups with clear edge.", "source": "book:livermore", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "patience", "rule:liv-05"], "author": "Edwin Lef\u00e8vre / Jesse Livermore", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Know what you own and why you own it.", "source": "book:lynch", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["fundamentals", "conviction", "rule:lyn-01"], "author": "Peter Lynch", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Avoid hot tips and stocks 'everyone' is talking about.", "source": "book:lynch", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["psychology", "sentiment", "rule:lyn-02"], "author": "Peter Lynch", "triggers": ["sentiment=euphoric"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Small caps with strong earnings growth often outperform.", "source": "book:lynch", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["fundamentals", "growth", "rule:lyn-03"], "author": "Peter Lynch", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "It's futile to predict the economy; predict the company.", "source": "book:lynch", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["fundamentals", "rule:lyn-04"], "author": "Peter Lynch", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Selling winners too soon and holding losers is the cardinal sin.", "source": "book:lynch", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "trade_mgmt", "rule:lyn-05"], "author": "Peter Lynch", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Always buy with a margin of safety.", "source": "book:graham", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["fundamentals", "risk", "rule:gra-01"], "author": "Benjamin Graham", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Mr. Market is moody \u2014 exploit his swings, don't follow him.", "source": "book:graham", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["psychology", "sentiment", "rule:gra-02"], "author": "Benjamin Graham", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Investment is most intelligent when most businesslike.", "source": "book:graham", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "process", "rule:gra-03"], "author": "Benjamin Graham", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "The investor's chief problem is likely to be himself.", "source": "book:graham", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["psychology", "rule:gra-04"], "author": "Benjamin Graham", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Distinguish investment from speculation; never confuse the two.", "source": "book:graham", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["risk", "classification", "rule:gra-05"], "author": "Benjamin Graham", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Risk control is the most important attribute of a successful trader.", "source": "book:schwager", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["risk", "rule:sch-01"], "author": "Jack Schwager", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Develop an edge before sizing up; method before money.", "source": "book:schwager", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["process", "risk", "rule:sch-02"], "author": "Jack Schwager", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Discipline is the bridge between strategy and results.", "source": "book:schwager", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "process", "rule:sch-03"], "author": "Jack Schwager", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "The trade you don't take can save more than the trade you do.", "source": "book:schwager", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["psychology", "patience", "rule:sch-04"], "author": "Jack Schwager", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Lose your opinion, not your money \u2014 adapt to evidence.", "source": "book:schwager", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "adaptation", "rule:sch-05"], "author": "Jack Schwager", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Cut losses at 7-8% \u2014 no exceptions.", "source": "book:oneil", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["risk", "trade_mgmt", "rule:one-01"], "author": "William O'Neil", "triggers": ["unrealized_pct<-7"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Buy strong earnings (current quarter EPS up 25%+).", "source": "book:oneil", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["fundamentals", "growth", "rule:one-02"], "author": "William O'Neil", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Buy stocks making new 52-week highs from sound bases.", "source": "book:oneil", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["pattern", "breakout", "rule:one-03"], "author": "William O'Neil", "triggers": ["near_52w_high"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Volume should expand on breakout \u2014 50%+ above average.", "source": "book:oneil", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["pattern", "volume", "rule:one-04"], "author": "William O'Neil", "triggers": ["rvol>1.5"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Trade with the market trend, not against it.", "source": "book:oneil", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["trend", "regime", "rule:one-05"], "author": "William O'Neil", "triggers": ["regime=bear"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Think in probabilities, not certainties.", "source": "book:douglas", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["psychology", "probability", "rule:dou-01"], "author": "Mark Douglas", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Each trade is independent \u2014 don't let prior outcomes bias you.", "source": "book:douglas", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "rule:dou-02"], "author": "Mark Douglas", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "A consistent process produces consistent results.", "source": "book:douglas", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["process", "psychology", "rule:dou-03"], "author": "Mark Douglas", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Anything can happen \u2014 accept uncertainty as the only certainty.", "source": "book:douglas", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "risk", "rule:dou-04"], "author": "Mark Douglas", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "You don't need to know what will happen to make money.", "source": "book:douglas", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["psychology", "probability", "rule:dou-05"], "author": "Mark Douglas", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Don't fight the tape \u2014 ride confirmed trends.", "source": "book:covel", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["trend", "rule:cov-01"], "author": "Michael Covel", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Most trades will be small losers; a few will be big winners.", "source": "book:covel", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["risk", "expectancy", "rule:cov-02"], "author": "Michael Covel", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Exit rules matter more than entry rules.", "source": "book:covel", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["trade_mgmt", "risk", "rule:cov-03"], "author": "Michael Covel", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Diversify across uncorrelated markets to smooth equity curve.", "source": "book:covel", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["risk", "diversification", "rule:cov-04"], "author": "Michael Covel", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Don't predict \u2014 react to price.", "source": "book:covel", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["trend", "process", "rule:cov-05"], "author": "Michael Covel", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Diversify across uncorrelated bets \u2014 the holy grail of investing.", "source": "book:dalio", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["risk", "diversification", "rule:dal-01"], "author": "Ray Dalio", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Pain + reflection = progress; analyze every loss.", "source": "book:dalio", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["process", "learning", "rule:dal-02"], "author": "Ray Dalio", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Don't confuse a good outcome with a good decision (or vice versa).", "source": "book:dalio", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "process", "rule:dal-03"], "author": "Ray Dalio", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Know what kind of regime you're in (growth/inflation rising/falling).", "source": "book:dalio", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["regime", "macro", "rule:dal-04"], "author": "Ray Dalio", "triggers": ["regime=unknown"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "The biggest risk is the one you don't see \u2014 stress-test for tails.", "source": "book:dalio", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["risk", "tail", "rule:dal-05"], "author": "Ray Dalio", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "When you're sure you're right, bet big \u2014 but verify the thesis daily.", "source": "book:soros", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["conviction", "sizing", "rule:sor-01"], "author": "George Soros", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Reflexivity: prices influence fundamentals which influence prices.", "source": "book:soros", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["sentiment", "macro", "rule:sor-02"], "author": "George Soros", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "It's not whether you're right or wrong \u2014 it's how much you make when right and lose when wrong.", "source": "book:soros", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["risk", "expectancy", "rule:sor-03"], "author": "George Soros", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "When the thesis breaks, exit immediately \u2014 don't rationalize.", "source": "book:soros", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["trade_mgmt", "psychology", "rule:sor-04"], "author": "George Soros", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Markets reward those who recognize regime change first.", "source": "book:soros", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["regime", "adaptation", "rule:sor-05"], "author": "George Soros", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Risk means more things can happen than will happen.", "source": "book:marks", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["risk", "probability", "rule:mar-01"], "author": "Howard Marks", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Second-level thinking beats first-level thinking \u2014 always ask 'and then what?'", "source": "book:marks", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["psychology", "process", "rule:mar-02"], "author": "Howard Marks", "triggers": [], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "The most dangerous words: 'It's different this time.'", "source": "book:marks", "confidence": 0.95, "tags": ["psychology", "sentiment", "rule:mar-03"], "author": "Howard Marks", "triggers": ["sentiment=euphoric"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "Buy fear, sell greed \u2014 be contrarian when sentiment is extreme.", "source": "book:marks", "confidence": 0.85, "tags": ["sentiment", "contrarian", "rule:mar-04"], "author": "Howard Marks", "triggers": ["vix>30", "vix<13"], "active": true}
{"ts": "2026-05-03T07:35:30", "text": "It's not what you buy, it's what you pay \u2014 entry price is everything.", "source": "book:marks", "confidence": 0.9, "tags": ["fundamentals", "entry", "rule:mar-05"], "author": "Howard Marks", "triggers": [], "active": true}
